Package: rflow
Type: Package
Title: A Native R Workflow Orchestrator Inspired by Apache Airflow
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("Jorge Valente", "Hernandez Castelan", email = "valentehcastelan@hotmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: rflow is a lightweight, dependency-graph-based workflow orchestrator
    written entirely in R, inspired by Apache Airflow. It lets you define DAGs
    (Directed Acyclic Graphs) of tasks using idiomatic R (R6 objects, the
    magrittr-style %>>% operator, and plain R functions as task bodies), execute
    them sequentially or in parallel via the 'future' package, persist run/task
    state to a SQLite metadata database exactly like Airflow's metadata DB, retry
    failed tasks, template task parameters with execution-date macros, and inspect
    everything through an interactive Shiny "webserver" UI with a DAG graph view,
    Gantt chart, and task logs, all without leaving R or touching Python.
